// CROWN refinement (P0, 2026-10-01): an UNANNOTATED parameter handed
// straight to a refined one acquires that precondition (the inference the
// wheel leans on), and with it the guard. `caller`'s `m` is inferred
// Positive; `outer`'s argument claim against it is open, so the trap
// `inv`'s division guards is outer's to pay. Expect E_EffectMismatch at outer.
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn inv(n: Positive) = 100 / n

fn caller(m) = inv(m)

fn outer(k) with !Trap = caller(k + 1)

fn main() = outer(0 - 1)
